    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S3834A\n\nSPONSOR: ADDABBO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to providing notice to\nschool districts and nonpublic schools located in a city with a popu-\nlation of one million or more of certain construction projects\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo require the written notification to a school district 14 days prior\nto the commencement of a construction project that may disrupt the traf-\nfic to and from a school.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Section 102 of the highway law is amended by adding a new\nsubdivision 19 to require the written notice to a school district with\nregard to the construction of a building, alteration, public utility\nimprovement or extension of a highway, sidewalk or appurtenance.\n\nSubsection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThere have been complaints by school districts that roadways and side-\nwalks outside of school buildings have been dug to install gas lines or\npiping which has caused hazardous conditions for the students, teachers\nand staff who enter and exit the school buildings.  In many cases, the\nschool superintendent or principal were never informed of the planned\nconstruction. By requiring 14 days notice to the school district, the\nprincipal or other school staff in charge can plan accordingly to ensure\nsafe access and exit from the school building. The 14 day notification\nrequirement would not apply in the event of emergency situations.\n\n \nAMENDMENT NOTE:\n\nAdded Non-public schools\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019 - S. 3079 - Referred to Senate Transportation Committee.\n\n2020 - S. 3079A - Referred to Senate Transportation Committee.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
